_CONNECTIONS`, checked when `constants.py` is imported) handler threads exist at once. A thread counts from the moment the server hands it a connection until it ends, so the reply write, the draining and the follow-up after the reply count too (the 256 limit counts only the reading part). At that limit the new connection gets the same complete 503 busy and nothing is stored. At start-up the open-file limit must cover about 3 files per handler thread (`FDS_PER_HANDLER_THREAD`) plus `FD_RESERVE` (64). If the follow-up cannot open a connection because the desk is out of file handles (`EMFILE`/`ENFILE`), nothing was sent: the row goes back to `pending` with `last_error` `no_descriptors` and no automatic try is used up.
